{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2789 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "477a29f8f98e3700e439d96ec21d77b26ef3885e9221ac486facbb7dec816b26" :edb/db-before-t 2788 :edb/db-after-t 2789 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536101 50 #inst "2026-10-09T15:00:13.745Z" 13194139536101 true] [17592186171975 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383656 13194139536101 true] [17592186171975 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383663 13194139536101 true] [17592186171975 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383670 13194139536101 true] [17592186171976 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383677 13194139536101 true] [17592186172578 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536101 true] [17592186172578 1100 "An object moves along a circular path with position $r(t) = 3(\\cos 2ti + \\sin 2tj)$ meters. Find the magnitude of the acceleration of the object at time $t$, measured in seconds." 13194139536101 false] [17592186172578 1100 "An object moves along a circular path with position $r(t)=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j)$ meters. Find the magnitude of the acceleration of the object at time $t,$ measured in seconds." 13194139536101 true] [17592186172578 1145 "**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we find the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(r(t))^{′} \\\\  & =(3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j))^{′} \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the acceleration vector by differentiating the velocity vector. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =(v(t))^{′} \\\\  & =(-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i+6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j)^{′} \\\\  & =-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the magnitude of the acceleration as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}||a(t)|| & =\\sqrt{(-12\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+(-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144{cos}^{2}⁡2t+144{sin}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{144} \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude of the acceleration is $12\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nNote that $||a||$ is constant, but $a$ is not. \n\n**Method 2**\n\nFor uniform circular motion in the $xy$-plane, we have\n\n$$\na=-{\\omega }^{2}r\\,⇒\\,||a||={\\omega }^{2}||r||.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the radius of the circle is $a=3\\,\\text{m}$ and the angular frequency $\\omega =2\\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n||a||={2}^{2}\\cdot 3=12\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383656 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383657 13194139536101 true] [17592186383656 1089 "q-97640" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383656 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536101 true] [17592186383656 1100 "An object moves along a circular path with position $r(t)=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j$ meters. Find the speed of the object at time $t,$ measured in seconds." 13194139536101 true] [17592186383656 1113 #uuid "f995a141-d20e-5cb4-a7c5-cd9ca5ffca15" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383656 1145 "**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we find the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(r(t))^{′} \\\\  & =(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j)^{′} \\\\  & =-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, we calculate the magnitude of the velocity vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}||v(t)|| & =\\sqrt{(-10\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}+(10\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100{sin}^{2}⁡2t+100{cos}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100({sin}^{2}⁡2t+{cos}^{2}⁡2t)} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the object is $10\\text{ m/s}.$\n\nNote that the speed is constant, but the velocity is not. \n\n**Method 2**\n\nFor uniform circular motion in the $xy$-plane, we have\n\n$$\n||v||=R|\\omega |,\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the radius of the circle, and $\\omega $ is the angular velocity.\n\nIn our case, the radius of the circle is $R=5\\,\\text{m}$ and the angular frequency $\\omega =2\\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n||v||=5\\cdot |2|=10\\text{ m/s}.\n$$" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383658 13194139536101 true] [17592186383657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383659 13194139536101 true] [17592186383657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383660 13194139536101 true] [17592186383657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383661 13194139536101 true] [17592186383657 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383662 13194139536101 true] [17592186383657 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536101 true] [17592186383657 1041 "selection" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383657 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383662 13194139536101 true] [17592186383657 1110 #uuid "a74df77b-4150-572f-9be4-27e6f134b802" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383658 1034 "5\\text{ m/s}" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383658 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383658 1111 #uuid "c15f4d60-adc8-5f48-93d0-28bd34b73911" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383659 1034 "100\\text{ m/s}" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383659 1111 #uuid "fa7602ad-c2b9-51a6-b631-7002a8be6489" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383660 1034 "25\\text{ m/s}" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383660 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383660 1111 #uuid "98f7da3d-695b-564d-a747-2c679c13e042" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383661 1034 "20\\text{ m/s}" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383661 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383661 1111 #uuid "67d8e66b-06f1-5a2a-bbe3-fe6b8b1c4af3" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383662 1034 "10\\text{ m/s}" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383662 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383662 1111 #uuid "b37a6afd-5db8-50e9-961e-b4f414b5f20c" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383663 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383664 13194139536101 true] [17592186383663 1089 "q-97664" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383663 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536101 true] [17592186383663 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along a counterclockwise circular path centered at $O$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity of $1\\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Given that the particle is located at $(5,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the velocity of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ seconds." 13194139536101 true] [17592186383663 1113 #uuid "af2083e0-3aeb-5fcd-b845-0a22c5b82e0f" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383663 1145 "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nIn our case, we have $R=5$ and $\\omega =1\\text{ rad/s},$ so we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j))^{′} \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the velocity vector at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,i+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,j \\\\  & =-5\\,i\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383664 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383665 13194139536101 true] [17592186383664 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383666 13194139536101 true] [17592186383664 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383667 13194139536101 true] [17592186383664 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383668 13194139536101 true] [17592186383664 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383669 13194139536101 true] [17592186383664 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536101 true] [17592186383664 1041 "selection" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383664 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383666 13194139536101 true] [17592186383664 1110 #uuid "f4fab373-9ee1-5e7e-a84b-8966c502f0a9" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383665 1034 "5\\,i" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383665 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383665 1111 #uuid "b5fee7da-6127-585a-97ea-f2c5a3223789" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383666 1034 "-5\\,i" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383666 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383666 1111 #uuid "f3fa6663-8feb-5ad2-ba1a-4930a76f7e92" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383667 1034 "-5\\,i+5\\,j" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383667 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383667 1111 #uuid "b5585aff-8803-5b22-8c1e-10672966d7b8" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383668 1034 "-5\\,j" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383668 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383668 1111 #uuid "7242a4c6-56f5-50ba-98a5-8cb5a5f40104" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383669 1034 "5\\,i-5\\,j" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383669 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383669 1111 #uuid "2e714924-30fe-5199-b18e-07fe3083024b" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383670 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383671 13194139536101 true] [17592186383670 1089 "q-97666" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383670 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536101 true] [17592186383670 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along a counterclockwise circular path centered at $O$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity of $2\\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Given that the particle is located at $(4,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the velocity of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$ seconds." 13194139536101 true] [17592186383670 1113 #uuid "ba9f4197-bf38-5147-a088-adef74f86d38" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383670 1145 "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $R$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(R,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nIn our case, we have $R=4$ and $\\omega =2\\text{ rad/s},$ so we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the velocity vector by differentiating the position vector. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j))^{′} \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,i+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the velocity vector at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{8},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})\\,i+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})\\,j \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,i+8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,j \\\\  & =-\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,i+\\frac{8\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,j \\\\  & =-4\\sqrt{2}\\,i+4\\sqrt{2}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383671 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383672 13194139536101 true] [17592186383671 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383673 13194139536101 true] [17592186383671 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383674 13194139536101 true] [17592186383671 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383675 13194139536101 true] [17592186383671 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383676 13194139536101 true] [17592186383671 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536101 true] [17592186383671 1041 "selection" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383671 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383672 13194139536101 true] [17592186383671 1110 #uuid "3455a640-7273-5520-909a-98c567b13358" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383672 1034 "-4\\sqrt{2}i+4\\sqrt{2}j" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383672 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383672 1111 #uuid "15fcce13-48c6-5960-badd-3dd42e6d880a" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383673 1034 "4\\sqrt{2}i" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383673 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383673 1111 #uuid "2eb3d382-8090-59c2-9dad-ab4eb83382ee" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383674 1034 "-8\\sqrt{2}j" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383674 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383674 1111 #uuid "35411343-0b0a-526d-8c1a-315e6230dd93" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383675 1034 "4\\sqrt{2}i-4j" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383675 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383675 1111 #uuid "8986bcae-209d-5922-9f41-86f75dcc8433" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383676 1034 "-4i+4\\sqrt{2}j" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383676 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383676 1111 #uuid "80023cdb-5d7d-5efc-9e16-1785239ad288" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383677 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383678 13194139536101 true] [17592186383677 1089 "q-97674" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383677 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536101 true] [17592186383677 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along a counterclockwise circular path centered at $O$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity of $0.5\\,\\text{rad/s}.$ Given that the particle is located at $(4,0)$ when $t=0,$ find the acceleration of the particle at $t=\\pi $ seconds." 13194139536101 true] [17592186383677 1113 #uuid "0c4456dd-d406-5a8c-9a07-35ca3a15f591" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383677 1145 "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $a$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=a(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(a,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=4$ and $\\omega =\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ rad/s},$ so we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,i+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the velocity and acceleration vectors by differentiating. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & ={(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,i+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,j)}^{′} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,j \\\\ a(t) & ={(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,j)}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{t}{2}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the acceleration vector at $t=\\pi ,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(\\pi ) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\,j \\\\  & =-\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383678 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383679 13194139536101 true] [17592186383678 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383680 13194139536101 true] [17592186383678 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383681 13194139536101 true] [17592186383678 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383682 13194139536101 true] [17592186383678 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383683 13194139536101 true] [17592186383678 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536101 true] [17592186383678 1041 "selection" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383678 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383683 13194139536101 true] [17592186383678 1110 #uuid "8f709cf3-8702-56fb-b86d-447224d66cb4" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383679 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}\\,i" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383679 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383679 1111 #uuid "a4808dc6-0ae7-5ba9-ab08-c458e6ae63db" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383680 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}\\,j" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383680 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383680 1111 #uuid "8fdbe17d-914d-52b9-88d8-79ab2652cb56" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383681 1034 "2\\,j" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383681 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383681 1111 #uuid "3f187c12-f580-54c1-8168-8a3d342e82be" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383682 1034 "-2\\,i+2\\,j" 13194139536101 true] [17592186383682 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536101 true] [17592186383682 1111 #uuid "8a0adcb8-b3cc-5956-8f77-c047b